{
 "about": "Which clip a shared or pasted text names. The page's parseLink (engine/crate.html) and the share extension's SharedInbox.shareLink (ios/Addify/SharedInbox.swift) read text by the same rule, so a share and a paste of the same text scan the same clip. engine/test_round7c.py, engine/test_round8c.py and engine/test_round9c.py check parseLink against every case here.",
 "rule": [
  "1. Every http(s) link in the text is a candidate, in order; the first candidate that is a clip wins (unchanged).",
  "2. With no http(s) link, the leading run of URL characters (leading characters in strip_leading dropped first, trailing characters in strip_trailing dropped after; the whole text when that run is empty) is the next candidate (unchanged).",
  "3. ROUND 7C, ROUND 8C, ROUND 9C: with no clip from steps 1 and 2 (whether or not the text holds http(s) links), split the text into words on the separators below. For each word, in order: remove every zero-width character, then search the word for its first TikTok or Instagram host with word_search (so a host glued to the word before it is found: an emoji, an em dash, a colon or a full-width colon before it), skip the match when word_search_skip says it sits in another link (ROUND 9C), then cut the match at the first character not in url_chars, then drop the trailing characters in strip_trailing, then read it with the clip test (https:// is added). The first word that is a clip wins. A word whose match is a TikTok or Instagram page (not a clip) is kept as the word page; only the first one counts.",
  "4. A profile, sound, tag, story or other page link, or another site's link, never wins over a clip anywhere in the text (ROUND 8C: an http(s) page or other link before or after a clip written without https:// included). With no clip anywhere, the result is no clip; the page then names the app of a page link found in step 1 or 2, else (ROUND 9C) the app of the first word page from step 3 ('page'), so 'omg tiktok.com/@u lol' names TikTok as its https form does. The share extension hands that page link over (https:// added)."
 ],
 "separators": "Unicode White_Space: U+0009-U+000D, U+0020, U+0085, U+00A0, U+1680, U+2000-U+200A, U+2028, U+2029, U+202F, U+205F, U+3000",
 "zero_width": [
  "U+200B",
  "U+200C",
  "U+200D",
  "U+2060",
  "U+FEFF"
 ],
 "strip_leading": "([{<\"'",
 "strip_trailing": ".,;:!?'\"()[]{}<>*",
 "url_chars": "A-Z a-z 0-9 - . _ ~ : / ? # [ ] @ ! $ & ' ( ) * + , ; = % (the characters LINK_RE reads as part of a link)",
 "word_search": "(?:^|[^A-Za-z0-9.-])((?:[a-z0-9-]+\\.)*(?:tiktok\\.com|instagram\\.com|instagr\\.am)\\/\\S*) (JavaScript, ignoring case; the link is group 1)",
 "word_search_skip": "ROUND 9C: the run of url_chars right before the match's group 1 (back to the start of the word or to the last character not in url_chars) holds another host name and then a / or ?, as /[A-Za-z0-9-]\\.[A-Za-z0-9-].*[\\/?]/ finds: the host is in that link's path or query ('example.com/tiktok.com/...', 'evil.com/?u=tiktok.com/...', 'google.com/search?q=tiktok.com/...'), so the word has no TikTok or Instagram host. A host after an emoji or any other character not in url_chars is not in it ('youtube.com/watch?v=x<emoji>tiktok.com/...'), nor one after a scheme alone ('https:/www.instagram.com/reel/...').",
 "clip_shapes": "tiktok.com (www., m.): /@user/video/<6-25 digits>, /@user/photo/<6-25 digits>, /t/<5-16 alnum>, /v/<6-25 digits>(.html); vm.tiktok.com or vt.tiktok.com: /<5-16 alnum> or /t/<5-16 alnum>; instagram.com or instagr.am (www., m.): /(<user>/)(reel|reels|p|tv)/<5-40 code>. A trailing slash is allowed. instagr.am is handed on as www.instagram.com.",
 "fields": {
  "clip": "the link parseLink hands on to the scan, exactly, or null when the text names no clip",
  "key": "the video that link names: https:// + host in lower case without www. or m. + path without its trailing slash, no query (the page's stripClip). A port that hands on another spelling of the same link matches on key",
  "page": "with no clip: the app whose page link the page names in its 'not a clip' message (TikTok or Instagram), else null"
 },
